  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Muammar Gaddafi was the Libyan military ruler who overthrew King Idris in 1969 and remained in power until 2011. He chaired the Revolutionary Command Council and later governed under the title Leader of the Revolution. The author of The Green Book, he reshaped Libya's institutions around his own system of government.",
    "html": "<p>Muammar Gaddafi was the Libyan military ruler who overthrew King Idris in 1969 and remained in power until 2011. He chaired the Revolutionary Command Council and later governed under the title Leader of the Revolution. The author of The Green Book, he reshaped Libya's institutions around his own system of government.</p>\r\n",
