  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Libyan ruler Muammar Gaddafi grew up in a herding family near Sirte and completed his secondary education in Misurata. He entered the military academy in Benghazi and encouraged members of his clandestine movement to enrol alongside him. After further training in Britain, he served as a lieutenant in the Signal Corps.\n\nHe invited African leaders to an extraordinary summit in Sirte in 1999. The resulting declaration committed them to establish the African Union and instructed ministers to prepare its founding legal text. Gaddafi later served a one-year term as the Union's chair, representing Libya in its rotating leadership.",
    "html": "<p>Libyan ruler Muammar Gaddafi grew up in a herding family near Sirte and completed his secondary education in Misurata. He entered the military academy in Benghazi and encouraged members of his clandestine movement to enrol alongside him. After further training in Britain, he served as a lieutenant in the Signal Corps.</p>\r\n<p>He invited African leaders to an extraordinary summit in Sirte in 1999. The resulting declaration committed them to establish the African Union and instructed ministers to prepare its founding legal text. Gaddafi later served a one-year term as the Union's chair, representing Libya in its rotating leadership.</p>\r\n",
